From: LuneOS <webos-ports@googlegroups.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] db: run the backup/restore callbacks with admin privilege

MojDbServiceHandlerBase::invokeImpl() always constructs MojDbReq(false),
so MojDb::dump()'s `if (!req->admin())` check rejects every caller that
reaches internal/preBackup over the bus - the reply is
"db: access denied" (MojErrDbAccessDenied) no matter who asks.  The same
applies to the object/kind puts that internal/postRestore performs
through MojDb::load().

That makes the whole /etc/palm/backup callback protocol dead code on the
bus: db8 ships src/db-luna/backup-com.palm.db advertising those four
methods, and nothing can successfully call two of them.  webOS 3.0.5
gated this on an admin role list read from /etc/palm/mojodb.conf; db8
3.2.0 has no such file and no replacement, it simply denies everyone.

Access control for these methods already exists and is enforced one
layer up: ls-hubd only routes them for callers holding the
"database.management" ACG group (see
files/sysbus/com.webos.service.db.api.json.in).  Elevating the request
inside the two handlers restores the intended behaviour without widening
what the hub lets through.

Needed by com.palm.app.backup (woce-backup), which is the first consumer
of the backup protocol on LuneOS.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [LuneOS specific]
---
--- a/src/db/MojDbServiceHandlerInternal.cpp
+++ b/src/db/MojDbServiceHandlerInternal.cpp
@@ -131,6 +131,13 @@
 MojErr MojDbServiceHandlerInternal::handlePostRestore(MojServiceMessage* msg, MojObject& payload, MojDbReq& req)
 {
     LOG_TRACE("Entering function %s", __FUNCTION__);
+	// The backup/restore callbacks are the platform's own backup protocol
+	// (registered via /etc/palm/backup) and are already gated on the
+	// database.management ACG group by the hub. MojDbServiceHandlerBase
+	// always builds a non-admin MojDbReq, so without this guard
+	// MojDb::dump()/put() reject every bus caller and the API is dead code.
+	MojDbAdminGuard adminGuard(req);
+
 	MojAssert(msg);
 
 	MojString dir;
@@ -163,6 +170,13 @@
 MojErr MojDbServiceHandlerInternal::handlePreBackup(MojServiceMessage* msg, MojObject& payload, MojDbReq& req)
 {
     LOG_TRACE("Entering function %s", __FUNCTION__);
+	// The backup/restore callbacks are the platform's own backup protocol
+	// (registered via /etc/palm/backup) and are already gated on the
+	// database.management ACG group by the hub. MojDbServiceHandlerBase
+	// always builds a non-admin MojDbReq, so without this guard
+	// MojDb::dump()/put() reject every bus caller and the API is dead code.
+	MojDbAdminGuard adminGuard(req);
+
 	MojAssert(msg);
 
 	MojErr err;
